    questions: [{"prompt":"Best scientific approach for this lesson (Design or analyze a reaction investigation with quantitative claims.…)?","choices":["Replace evidence with a slogan.","Use a labeled model and evidence to apply “Reactions Unit Lab CER.”","Memorize the title only.","Change multiple variables at once and call it proof."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Models + evidence beat slogans.","order":1},{"prompt":"Which term is most central in Unit 8 for “Reactions Unit Lab CER”?","choices":["random guessing","ignoring units/labels","coefficient","mole ratio"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Emphasizes “coefficient.”","order":2},{"prompt":"You find a contradiction with your first explanation. Best next move?","choices":["Erase everything and invent a new story.","Keep the slogan if it sounds confident.","Hide conflicting data.","Name the broken step, revise the model, and re-check against evidence."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Revision is a scientific virtue.","order":3}],
